triage: revise_rules: The game was built correctly, but the design fails evaluation on two counts. A round has 6 choice steps against a limit of 4, and a thoughtless 'always take the first option' policy wins about 77–80% of its games from either seat while 'always take the last option' loses about 75–80%, so a trivial strategy dominates.
